{
  "rationale": "Use a minimal plant split into sensing and motion, then a small policy specification with one-shot action states. Clear exploration defaults to random_walk, obstacle events force dedicated turn-recovery states, and path_clear returns quickly to exploration. Action states self-loop on path_clear so uncontrollables do not preempt the intended pulse, while safety-critical obstacle events redirect immediately.",
  "strategy": [
    "Model sensing as an uncontrollable environment plant and motion as a controllable capability plant",
    "Use a compact supervisor specification with clear, forward-progress, and obstacle-recovery states",
    "Bias exploration toward random_walk in clear space, insert short move_forward pulses after clear sensing, and use directed turns for side/front obstacles",
    "Keep obstacle-recovery states one-shot and forbid move_forward/random_walk there"
  ],
